--- !u!114 &194576646
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 194576644}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 1f3ef889599182844a2f5643151998e9, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  storyText: {fileID: 1920307469}
  fullText: "Ang Kwento ng Tikbalang\n\n\u201CAte, is it true that Tikbalangs exist?
    Isn\u2019t that just a way to scare kids into behaving?\u201D Edith asked her
    eldest sister.\n\n\u201CBut Uncle Jose said they really do exist. He even said
    he was there when they caught one.\u201D\n\n\u201CCome on Ate, tell us what happened,\u201D
    the youngest, Teresa, pleaded.\n\n\u201CAlright, come here and listen.\u201D\n\nThere
    was once a very beautiful young woman named Linda in Uncle Jose\u2019s village.
    Many men courted her because she was not only beautiful but also kind.\n\nHowever,
    despite all the men in the village who admired her, none won her heart. \n\nOne
    day, she met a young man from Manila named Roberto. He was handsome, tall, and
    seemingly respectable. \n\nMany village girls were attracted to Roberto, but
    he only had eyes for Linda.\n\nThe young man's courtship was met with Linda\u2019s
    love, and before long, they were married. Joyful days followed for the couple,
    who cherished each other deeply.\n\nTheir love was blessed with a beautiful baby
    girl named Ligaya. But dark clouds soon gathered over their peaceful life\u2014Linda
    fell ill and eventually passed away. \n\nRoberto was left in deep sorrow, with
    only their infant daughter to comfort him.\n\nOne night, while Roberto was feeding
    the baby with a bottle, he sensed someone behind him. \n\nTo his shock, he saw
    Linda standing at the bedroom door\u2014the same Linda who had just been buried
    the previous week. \n\nShe didn\u2019t speak, but stretched out her arms as if
    asking for the baby.\n\n\u201CNo, Linda, you\u2019re dead. This isn\u2019t right!\u201D
    Roberto said as he held the baby tighter and shook his head.\n\nThe woman left,
    but the next night she appeared again. Roberto refused even more firmly to give
    her the child. \n\nBut fear and confusion kept him from sleeping. When the same
    thing happened on the third night, he decided to consult the village elders.\n\n\u201CThat\u2019s
    not Linda\u2019s ghost, Roberto,\u201D one elder said. \n\n\u201CThat\u2019s
    a Tikbalang taking the form of your wife.\u201D \n\n\u201CThere are Tikbalangs
    in our fields. They sleep in lumbang trees during the day and roam at night.\u201D\n\n\u201CAre
    Tikbalangs real? I thought they were just stories,\u201D Roberto asked, bewildered.
    \n\n\u201CThey\u2019re real. Do you know Karyo, the half-wit? He ended up like
    that because a Tikbalang took him when he was a child.\u201D \n\n\u201CHe disappeared
    for two days and was found by his father under a lumbang tree.\u201D\n\n\u201COh
    no, what should I do? Each night it becomes more desperate to take the baby,\u201D
    Roberto said, nearly in tears.\n\n\u201CDon\u2019t worry, we\u2019ll prepare,\u201D
    the elder promised. \n\nThat night, at the same hour, the Tikbalang came again,
    still in the form of Linda. \n\nJust as it was about to grab the baby from Roberto\u2019s
    arms, men burst out of the room. \n\nStartled, the Tikbalang leapt out of the
    window. \n\nBut waiting outside were more men who grabbed its hair and tied it
    to a coconut tree. They beat it over and over until it cried out for mercy. \n\n\u201CForgive
    me! I\u2019ll leave your place, just let me go. I\u2019ll take all my followers
    with me. We\u2019ll go far away and never bother you again. Please have mercy!\u201D
    cried the Tikbalang. \n\nMoved by its cries and promise never to return, the
    village men released the creature.\n\nSince then, no Tikbalang has ever been
    seen again in the village. \n\nThe child, Ligaya, grew up to be a kind and beautiful
    woman like her mother. Even after marrying, she never left her father\u2019s
    side and cared for him until his old age.\n\n\u201CYour story was great, but
    scary, Ate,\u201D said Edith. \u201CWe might not be able to sleep.\u201D\n\n\u201CSay
    your prayers before bed,\u201D the eldest reminded with a teasing smile, \u201Cor
    the Tikbalang might pay you a visit!\u201D\n\n\u2013 THE END \u2013"
  previousRelic: {fileID: 30758455}
  nextRelic: {fileID: 1726128182}
